{
  "about": "What a chat's lines become as people use them (spec/chat.md). pins (Pins, Polls, Editing and unsending): a chat's `lines` by id in order, its `pins` the latest first, then one `step`: pin or unpin a line, unsend one (送信取消), or settle the poll a line carries (日にちを決める). `expected` is the pins after it, the latest first, and the one that made room for the new pin (`dropped`, for the app to say so), if any. The most pinned at once is design/src/chat.ts's chatRules.maxPins, 5. edited (Editing and unsending): a line with words and its link's page is given new words; `expected` says whether it keeps its page (`kept`) or takes the new words' (`new`). firstUnread (Unread lines and typing): who wrote each line, oldest first (`others`, `me`, or `app` for the app's own lines such as someone joining), and how many are unread; `expected` is the index of the line the chat opens on under ここから新着, null with nothing unread. Only others' lines count. writer (Unread lines and typing): whose a line is to the reader `me`, which every count of unread lines and ここから新着 go by: from its `author`, whether it is a `notice` from the app, and whether it is `hidden` (sent in a one-to-one chat by someone the reader blocked, never delivered); `expected` is `me`, `others` or `app`, the app's own and the undelivered ones never counted. directThread (One-to-one chats, spec/sync-protocol.md): two members' ids, given in either order; `expected` is their chat's thread id, the same from both sides: \"direct:\" and the two ids in order (by their UTF-16 code units, as every id is ASCII), joined by \":\". openingFrom (Unread lines and typing): the first line a chat lays out as it opens, from its `latest` line's seq and the reader's `read` mark (null for no reader): its latest page, back to the first unread line when that is earlier, at most chatRules.openMax lines (pageSize 50, openMax 200). firstComing (Unread lines and typing): when lines come in while the chat is open and following, the first of them it stops at under ここから新着 rather than going past: of the chat's `lines` (each a seq and who wrote it, as firstUnread counts them), the first after both the `latest` line it held before and the reader's `read` mark that others wrote; `expected` is its seq, null for none. Whether to stop there or go on to the foot is the screen's: when they fit, it goes on. readTo (Unread lines and typing): what the reader's `read` mark comes to as the chat's `lines` (each a seq and who wrote it, as firstUnread counts them) show: `shown` are the seqs of those whose foot is on the screen, in no particular order; `expected.read` is the mark after, the latest of them, never back (a line once on screen stays read), and `expected.unread` how many of others' lines are still unread past it, what ↓ counts. window (Unread lines and typing): the lines a chat lays out once it has opened, which stay as later lines come past a gap. The device `held` these runs of seqs (each its first and last), all others' lines but the reader's own (`mine`), the reader's `read` mark, and `from`, the first line laid out (null as the chat opens, openingFrom then choosing it). The lines laid out are those of the run holding the first line held at or after `from` (the latest run as the chat opens, laid out as openingFrom chooses, as with none held after it), from `from` to the run's last line; `expected.lines` are the first and last of them, `heldFrom` the run's first line, before which the server is asked for a page, `heldBefore` how many the device holds in the run before those laid out (laid out as the chat scrolls back without asking), `atEnd` whether they reach the latest line the device holds, and `unread` what ↓ counts: others' lines past the mark among them and after them, each line after them the device does not hold yet counted as unread. pageAfter (Unread lines and typing): while the lines laid out do not reach the latest the device holds, the page after them is asked as their foot nears, with the ChatPageRequest the earlier pages use: `before_seq` (`expected`) past the run's last line (`through`) by chatRules.pageSize and one, as a chat's seqs run without a gap on the server, so the page holds the lines straight after it, or near the latest the latest page, which reaches them too. draft (Drafts): what was being written in a chat, its `text` as it would be sent (mentions as <@id>), the line it answers (`replyTo`) or changes (`editing`) by seq, and the chat's `lines` the device holds then; `expected` is the draft kept, or opened again, or null when there is none to keep. withdrawn (Notifications): the chat lines' notifications a device has shown, each its `id`, chat (`groupId`, `threadId`) and line `seq`, and a `read` of one chat: its `readTo`, or null when the chat has no unread lines left; `expected` are the ids of those it takes back, in the order shown: the chat's, at or before readTo, all of the chat's for null. Another chat's, or a group's of the same thread name, stay. albums (Albums): a chat's `lines` in order, each with its `seq`, its `writer`, its `album` (empty for none), whether it is a `photo`, and whether it was `unsent`; `expected` is each album the chat draws, as its lines' seqs, only those of two photos or more (one left alone is drawn as a photo is). albumRows (Albums): how many photos an album has (`count`, 2 to chatRules.photosPerSend); `expected` is how many go in each of its rows, top first.",
  "pins": [
    {
      "name": "a pinned line comes first among the pins",
      "lines": ["a", "b"],
      "pins": ["a"],
      "step": {
        "pin": "b"
      },
      "expected": {
        "pins": ["b", "a"],
        "dropped": null
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "one pin past the most takes the place of the oldest",
      "lines": ["p0", "p1", "p2", "p3", "p4", "new"],
      "pins": ["p4", "p3", "p2", "p1", "p0"],
      "step": {
        "pin": "new"
      },
      "expected": {
        "pins": ["new", "p4", "p3", "p2", "p1"],
        "dropped": "p0"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "pinning a line already pinned only moves it up",
      "lines": ["p0", "p1", "p2", "p3", "p4"],
      "pins": ["p4", "p3", "p2", "p1", "p0"],
      "step": {
        "pin": "p0"
      },
      "expected": {
        "pins": ["p0", "p4", "p3", "p2", "p1"],
        "dropped": null
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "taking a pin off leaves the others",
      "lines": ["a", "b"],
      "pins": ["b", "a"],
      "step": {
        "unpin": "b"
      },
      "expected": {
        "pins": ["a"],
        "dropped": null
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a line taken back is not among the pins",
      "lines": ["a", "b"],
      "pins": ["b", "a"],
      "step": {
        "unsend": "a"
      },
      "expected": {
        "pins": ["b"],
        "dropped": null
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a settled poll is pinned, within the most pins",
      "lines": ["p0", "p1", "p2", "p3", "p4", "poll"],
      "pins": ["p4", "p3", "p2", "p1", "p0"],
      "step": {
        "settle": "poll"
      },
      "expected": {
        "pins": ["poll", "p4", "p3", "p2", "p1"],
        "dropped": "p0"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "settling a pinned poll again only moves its pin up",
      "lines": ["poll", "p0", "p1", "p2", "p3"],
      "pins": ["p3", "p2", "p1", "p0", "poll"],
      "step": {
        "settle": "poll"
      },
      "expected": {
        "pins": ["poll", "p3", "p2", "p1", "p0"],
        "dropped": null
      }
    }
  ],
  "edited": [
    {
      "name": "an edit keeps its link's page while the link stays",
      "text": "ここ https://cafe.example",
      "edit": "ここどう？ https://cafe.example",
      "expected": "kept"
    },
    {
      "name": "a second link added after the first keeps the first's page",
      "text": "https://cafe.example",
      "edit": "https://cafe.example か https://b.example",
      "expected": "kept"
    },
    {
      "name": "an edit that changes the link takes the new page",
      "text": "https://cafe.example",
      "edit": "https://b.example",
      "expected": "new"
    },
    {
      "name": "a new link put before the old one takes the new page",
      "text": "https://cafe.example",
      "edit": "https://b.example じゃなくて https://cafe.example",
      "expected": "new"
    },
    {
      "name": "an edit that removes the link takes the new words' page, none",
      "text": "ここ https://cafe.example",
      "edit": "やっぱりいいや",
      "expected": "new"
    }
  ],
